      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Are these multiple scenes in the same asset bundle? \n\nI've seen a bunch of worlds where items in the scene are aggressively shown and hidden depending on the player position, doesn't help with initial load time but does help with performance",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-10-01T14:12:32.566Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, when building a world in Unity for VRChat, we are limited to a single scene. This restriction poses challenges when it comes to controlling environmental elements like fog thickness.\n\n1. Improved Environmental Control: With multi-scene support, creators would have the ability to control environmental factors like fog thickness on a per-scene basis. This level of granularity would enable us to create more diverse and immersive environments within a single world.\n\n2. Enhanced Creativity: The ability to work with multiple scenes would empower creators to craft more complex and dynamic worlds, pushing the boundaries of what's possible in VRChat.\n\n3. Improved Loading Times: With multi-scene support, users would only need to load one scene at a time, greatly improving performance and reducing the wait time when transitioning between scenes. This would be especially beneficial in worlds with numerous scenes, where loading times can be a significant factor in user experience.\n\nWhile there may be additional advantages, my primary perspective on this suggestion revolves around world-building. I'd like to create more complex, well designed and unique worlds and having everything in one scene isn't ideal for achieving that.",
